### Attribution of External Code & Major Contributors
* **Third-Party Empirical PRC Code (`peleg-lab/led_firesync`):** The empirical firefly Phase Response Curve (PRC) mathematical formulation and helper functions (`wrap1`, `wrap_half`, `_alpha`, `R_tanh_step`, `Z_from_R`, and `make_tanh_prc`) used in `kuramoto_led_firesync_bifurcation.py` are **not original to this project**. They were taken directly from `simulation/prc_simulator.py` in the [`peleg-lab/led_firesync`](https://github.com/peleg-lab/led_firesync/blob/master/simulation/prc_simulator.py) GitHub repository developed by **Owen Martin, Nataliya Nechyporenko, Kaushik Jayaram, and Orit Peleg** (University of Colorado Boulder) as part of their study *Excitation–inhibition interactions mediate firefly flash synchronization* (Martin et al., 2026). Our contribution in `kuramoto_led_firesync_bifurcation.py` is limited to wrapping their empirical PRC factory into a vectorized $N = 100$ continuous-time ODE ensemble solver (`scipy.integrate.solve_ivp`) and rendering the resulting coupling sweep in Manim.
* **Theoretical & Pedagogical Foundation (Steven H. Strogatz):** The conceptual structure, bifurcation analysis, and undergraduate dynamical systems framing throughout this project rely heavily on **Steven H. Strogatz's** textbook *Nonlinear Dynamics and Chaos: With Applications to Physics, Biology, Chemistry, and Engineering* (3rd ed., 2024, CRC Press) and his foundational review *From Kuramoto to Crawford* (2000).
* **Visualization & Numerical Software (Manim Community & SciPy):** All mathematical animations and 3D phase-locking visualizations were rendered using **Manim** (Mathematical Animation Framework), developed and maintained by **The Manim Community Developers** (2026). Numerical integration of ordinary differential equations was performed using **SciPy** (`scipy.integrate.solve_ivp`, Virtanen et al., 2020).

